## ---- Card artwork (not tracked - see README) ----
# Each Set's card images live under Assets/Data/<License>/Cards/<Set>/Artwork/ - this is the
# multi-GB bulk of the project (card art for every license), deliberately excluded so the repo
# stays a code/config-only history. The small CardData .asset files sitting next to Artwork/ are
# still tracked - only the images themselves are skipped.
Assets/Data/**/Artwork/

# Card art loaded from Resources at runtime - separate bulk location from Assets/Data above,
# same reason for excluding it (multi-GB of card images, not code/config).
Assets/Resources/Cards/

# Per-set cover/booster art (small compared to the above, but still images - same "code-only
# repo" goal applies).
Assets/Art/

## ---- Unity crash-recovery data ----
# Auto-saved copies Unity creates after a crash/abnormal exit. Transient, not real project
# source, and can silently hold stale/unscrubbed data (e.g. an old copy of a scene made before
# a secret was removed from it) - excluded wholesale rather than audited file by file.
Assets/_Recovery/

## ---- Secrets - never commit these ----
# Your own Google OAuth credentials (see GameManager's Google Auth Config field / Data/
# GoogleAuthConfig.cs) - create this asset locally via Assets > Create > TCG Collector > Google
# Auth Config and fill in your real Client ID/Secret. It must never be committed - a MonoBehaviour
# field holding these directly (instead of a separate ignored asset) is what leaked a real secret
# into SampleScene.unity previously.
GoogleAuthConfig.asset
GoogleAuthConfig.asset.meta

## ---- Scratch / not project source ----
Claude outputs/
